abla	ilde{\phi}(z)}\le C$, because the gradients $ 
abla_z\eta_j (x-tz)$ and $
abla_z\gamma_0(x-tz)/\gamma_0(c_{B_j})$ give the factors $t(1+\mod{c_{B_j}})$ and $t\mod{x-tz}\gamma_0(x-tz)/\gamma_0(c_{B_j})$, respectively, both of which are bounded. This concludes the proof of Lemma ef{Lemma1}. \end{proof}
